    /**
     * Validate domain PTR records.
     *
     * This function validates the pointer records (PTR) for IPv4 and IPv6 addresses an account's domains send mail
     * from. It retrieves the PTR records for each IP address and determines which of the domain's IP addresses send
     * mail. It then validates the PTR records for each IP address and validates the A (IPv4) or AAAA (IPv6) records
     * pointing to each domain. This function also ensures that at least one of that domain's A or AAAA records points
     * back to the IP address.
     *
     * Documented: Available in cPanel & WHM 78 and later.
     *
     * Documented: Checks PTR records for sending IPv4/IPv6 addresses, matching A/AAAA records and forward-to-address
     * consistency. DNS records and nameservers remain payload data; the client does not perform separate DNS queries or
     * establish propagation.
     *
     * API-map identity: whm1:validate_current_ptrs#GET (wire name validate_current_ptrs; Mail DNS Settings).
     *
     * @param string|list<string> $domains The domain for which to validate the PTR records.
     * @return ValidateCurrentPtrsResult
     * @throws ApiException If transport, HTTP, the outcome, or the payload fails.
     * @throws PayloadMismatchException If the API reported success but the payload differs from the contract;
     *     any change the operation makes has already taken effect.
     * @throws InvalidArgumentException If a list argument is empty or contains non-strings.
